=begin rakudoc :!toc
=TITLE Introduction

This is a tool for editing RakuDoc v2 operating from a container. It is still under development, so new features will be added in due course.
The tool was tested using a recent version of the Firefox browser. Improvements are welcome via PRs.

Several source documents can be pulled from the container - these are listed in the drop-down box on the far left.

The documents include this introduction, the specification and exposition files for RakuDoc v2, a render test file, a citation sample file, and some tutorial files.

It is also possible to upload your own sources to the browser, edit them then download either the edited RakuDoc source or the rendered HTML.

=head User Interface

=numitem Select included file - click on B<Samples & tutorials>, which will pop up a drop down selection, choose the file you want.
=numitem Upload your own source - click on B<Upload>, which will pop up a file chooser interface that is dependent on your browser and OS. It is set to look for only files with the C<.rakudoc> file extension.
=numitem Download a file - click on B<Download>, which will pop up a form with a suggested filename and a default C<.rakudoc> extension.
The file name can be changed. Selecting the C<.rakudoc> file format will download the RakuDoc source, while selecting the C<.html> file format
will download the rendered HTML.

By default, RakuDoc source is sent to the container for rendering half a second after changes have been made in the source. Changes are not sent if
the browser has not received the most recent rendering (see the State indicator). For long files or when writing long sections of source, immediate rendering
can be distracting, so the Rendering process can be switched to I<manual>.
=counter item :!restart
=numitem Check the I<Render>B<Auto> setting by clicking on the B<Auto> button I<This is the default>.
Changes will be sent after a half second delay, unless rendering is proceeding.
=numitem Check the I<Render>B<Manual> setting by click on the B<Manual> button. Changes will not be sent.
=numitem Force a rendering by clicking on the B<Force rendering> button. Any changes will be send immediately, unless a previous rendering is being processed.

The RakuDoc renderer has two (currently) HTML renderers: a minimal rendering in which all the CSS and JS code are included in the file, and 
one that requires an online connection to access the Bulma CSS framework and online plugins. 
=counter item :!restart
=numitem Check the I<Framework>B<Minimal> setting by clicking on the B<Minimal> button I<This is the default>.
=numitem Check the I<Framework>B<Bulma & plugins> setting by click on the B<Bulma & plugins> button.
=numitem The state of the Rendering process is shown in I<State> section. There are four states:
=numitem2 I<Success> A rendering has been returned and was was successful in that an HTML file was created. Note, however, that errors in the RakuDoc 
may still exist, but these should be indicated in the warning section at the end of the rendering.
=numitem2 I<Failed> The RakuDoc source could not be parsed, and the parser message is returned.
=numitem2 I<Changes> Changes have been made in the RakuDoc source that have not been rendered. This will occur if the Render process has been toggled 
to I<Manual> and the source file has been edited, or changes have been made while a previous set of changes is still being rendered.
=numitem2 I<Processing> The renderer is still rendering the file. This will be shown when the latest changes have been sent to the Renderer, but the
rendered text has not been returned.

=end rakudoc